  "result": "Fixed. The bug was an off-by-one in `shop/pricing.py:10`. The check `line.qty > BULK_THRESHOLD` (threshold 10) only gave the discount from 11 units up, but the policy says 10 or more. I changed it to `>=`, a one-character fix. No other code compares against the threshold.\n\nAll 6 tests pass with `python3 -m unittest -v`. I didn't run the tests before the fix, but `test_bulk_discount` already covers exactly 10 units: it expects 1028 (1000 \u2212 5% = 950, plus 78 tax). Under the old check, 10 units got no discount and came to 1083, so that test was catching this bug.\n\nThe change isn't committed.",
